---
// A deliberately fictional rear-view camera, drawn as one registered SVG.
// The filled render and the technical drawing share the same coordinates, so
// scroll can reveal material and depth without swapping assets or changing the
// silhouette. The LCD opening is intentionally empty: MonitorFrame occupies
// the matching 420/385/760/420 box in this 1600×1000 viewBox. Keeping the
// LCD centred on the viewBox also keeps it centred in the viewport while it
// expands, so the scroll transition has no visible sideways drift.
---

<svg
  class="camera-illustration"
  viewBox="0 0 1600 1000"
  preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet"
  role="presentation"
  aria-hidden="true"
>
